The display transform in python/encino_waves/shaders/presentation.wgsl
adapts Khronos PBR Neutral from GLSL to WGSL, adds explicit exposure and
sRGB output conversion, and is distributed under the Apache License 2.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ToneMapping
License: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ToneMapping/blob/main/LICENSE.md

The analytical environment BRDF in ocean.wgsl follows Brian Karis's
"Physically Based Shading on Mobile" (Epic Games, 2014), with a bounded
dielectric smooth-surface limit. Epic's article permits use, modification,
and distribution of its code samples.
https://www.unrealengine.com/blog/physically-based-shading-on-mobile

Commercial HDR environments are supplied separately by the user. No Dutch
Skies images or other licensed environment data are distributed here.
